1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,242
Every egg carries an X chromosome. A sperm carries either an X or a Y.

2
00:00:04,242 --> 00:00:09,381
We model this by tossing a coin 100 times: heads for an X sperm, tails for a Y sperm.

3
00:00:09,381 --> 00:00:13,564
Predict: how many of the 100 'babies' will be girls? Pause and decide.

4
00:00:14,624 --> 00:00:17,850
Watch. After 20 tosses, there are 11 girls and 9 boys.

5
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:23,332
After 100 tosses, there are 48 girls and 52 boys: very close to half each.

6
00:00:24,392 --> 00:00:28,634
Explain what you saw. Half of all sperm carry an X and half carry a Y,

7
00:00:28,634 --> 00:00:32,697
so each baby has an equal chance of being XX, a girl, or XY, a boy.

8
00:00:32,697 --> 00:00:38,075
Small samples can be uneven, but with many tosses the result gets close to half and half.

9
00:00:38,075 --> 00:00:42,557
The father's sperm decides the sex. Pause and explain it in your own words.

10
00:00:43,616 --> 00:00:47,441
Inheritance is the passing of traits from parents to offspring.

11
00:00:47,441 --> 00:00:50,488
Sperm and egg cells have only 23 chromosomes each.

12
00:00:50,488 --> 00:00:56,224
At fertilisation their nuclei fuse, making a zygote with all 46 and a unique combination of DNA.

13
00:00:57,284 --> 00:01:01,467
One pair of chromosomes decides sex: females are XX and males are XY.

14
00:01:01,467 --> 00:01:04,992
Every egg carries an X, but a sperm can carry an X or a Y.

15
00:01:04,992 --> 00:01:09,773
So the father's sperm decides: X makes a girl, Y makes a boy, about fifty-fifty.

16
00:01:10,832 --> 00:01:15,374
The zygote divides into a ball of cells, which implants in the uterus wall.

17
00:01:15,374 --> 00:01:18,959
It's called an embryo until about nine weeks, then a fetus.

18
00:01:18,959 --> 00:01:24,695
If one zygote splits in two, we get identical twins; two separate eggs give non-identical twins.

19
00:01:25,755 --> 00:01:28,742
The fetus grows in the uterus for about 40 weeks.

20
00:01:28,742 --> 00:01:34,240
The placenta passes oxygen, nutrients and antibodies from the mother and takes away wastes.

21
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:39,080
The umbilical cord connects them, and the amnion and its fluid cushion the fetus.

22
00:01:40,139 --> 00:01:45,697
Harmful substances also cross the placenta, especially in the first weeks, when organs form.

23
00:01:45,697 --> 00:01:49,282
A balanced diet with folic acid, iron and calcium is vital.

24
00:01:49,282 --> 00:01:54,301
Smoking, alcohol and drugs can cause birth defects, low birth weight or miscarriage.
